[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186184219,
      "id": "fcbc10c0-4e6b-5dac-ad87-f0175e4a53d2",
      "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Using the Rank-Nullity Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4e65798d-ac5b-59a7-91bd-9ab9babcf743",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $4\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=1,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d29a1101-0712-58d0-8d57-055c0509a777",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
